Re-render Kab Hota Hai? (4 Main Triggers)
State Change (useState): Jab bhi aap setState function call karte hain aur state ki value change hoti hai, toh React component ko dobara render karta hai.

Props Change: Jab parent component se child component ko milne wale props change ho jate hain.

Parent Component Re-render: By default, jab bhi koi parent component re-render hota hai, toh uske andar ke saare child components bhi automatically re-render ho jate hain (chahe unke props change hue hon ya na hue hon).

Context Value Change: Agar aapne useContext use kiya hai aur Context ke andar ki value ya data change hota hai, toh us Context ko consume karne wale saare components re-render ho jate hain.

1-Line Interview Summary:
"Component tab re-render hota hai jab uski state change ho, uske props badlein, uska parent component re-render ho, ya koi related Context update ho."

Props change hon: Child ko naye props milne par woh usually re-render hota hai.

useRef ki value change ho: Sirf ref.current change karne se re-render nahi hota.

Normal variable change ho: Usse bhi automatically re-render nahi hota.

useEffect chale: Effect chalne se apne aap re-render nahi hota; lekin effect ke andar state update ho toh ho sakta hai.